      "problem": "The function $f(x,y)$ is defined as \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=x\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(y+1).\n$$\n\nEvaluate this function at the point $(-3,1).$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(-3,1),$ we substitute $x=-3$ and $y=1$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3,1) & =x\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(y+1)\\,{|}_{(-3,1)} \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(1+1) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{arccos}⁡2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined.",
